  "term": "branching",
  "definition": "In this source, branching means the growth of new neural offshoots or connections between cortical columns during offline brain activity such as sleep. The article also uses aberrant branching to mean unusually increased or misdirected connection growth, proposed there as part of autistic symptom development.",
